:Namespace SSEDemo
⍝ Server-Sent Events (SSE) demo for Jarvis: the CodeLocation for Samples/SSE (see README.md)
⍝
⍝ Endpoints
⍝   GET  /clock   the SSE stream (listed in SSEEndpoints). Each client receives:
⍝                   an unnamed welcome event when it connects        → EventSource "message" handler
⍝                   a "tick" event every second, with an id          → {"time":"12:34:56","clients":2}
⍝                   a "chat" event whenever anyone posts to /say     → {"name":"Ann","text":"hi","time":"12:34:56"}
⍝   POST /say     an ordinary JSON endpoint: {"name":"…","text":"…"} is broadcast to every client as a "chat" event
⍝
⍝ The ticker thread started by Initialize shows how application code outside any request can push events,
⍝ using Server.SSEConnections to find the open streams and Server.SendSSE to send to them.

    (⎕IO ⎕ML)←1 1

    Server←⍬          ⍝ the Jarvis instance, set by Initialize
    TickId←0          ⍝ id of the latest tick event; browsers send it back as Last-Event-ID when they reconnect
    TickerThread←⍬
    Stopping←0

    fmtTime←{,'ZI2,<:>,ZI2,<:>,ZI2'⎕FMT 1 3⍴3↑3↓⍵}   ⍝ ⎕TS → 'hh:mm:ss'
    trim←{⍵/⍨(∨\b)∧⌽∨\⌽b←' '≠⍵}                        ⍝ remove leading and trailing blanks

    ∇ r←Initialize server
    ⍝ AppInitFn: remember the server and start the ticker thread
      Server←server
      Stopping←0
      TickerThread←Ticker&1
      r←0
    ∇

    ∇ r←Shutdown
    ⍝ AppCloseFn: stop the ticker thread
      Stopping←1
      ⎕TKILL TickerThread
      r←0
    ∇

    ∇ r←clock req;last;msg;n
    ⍝ SSE endpoint function, called once for each new client, after the stream has started
    ⍝ req is the Request; the stream stays open while r is 0 (any other value closes it)
      n←≢Server.SSEConnections'clock'
      msg←'Welcome! ',(⍕n),((1+n=1)⊃' clients are' ' client is'),' connected'
      :If ~0∊⍴last←req.GetHeader'last-event-id' ⍝ a reconnecting browser tells us the last event it saw
          msg,←'. Welcome back: the last tick you saw was #',last
      :EndIf
      {}req Server.SendSSE msg ⍝ plain text → one unnamed "data:" event, to this client only
      r←0
    ∇

    ∇ r←say payload;name;text;data
    ⍝ ordinary JSON endpoint: broadcast a chat message to every client of /clock
      r←⎕NS''
      name←{0∊⍴⍵:'anonymous' ⋄ ⍵}40 limit payload'name'
      text←500 limit payload'text'
      :If 0∊⍴text
          →0⊣r.error←'text is required'
      :EndIf
      (data←⎕NS'').(name text time)←name text(fmtTime ⎕TS)
      r.sent←+/0=(Server.SSEConnections'clock')Server.SendSSE'chat'Server.FormatSSE data
    ∇

    ∇ r←max limit(ns name)
    ⍝ the trimmed text of field name in namespace ns, at most max characters ('' if it's missing)
      r←''
      :Trap 0
          r←trim,⍕ns⍎name
      :EndTrap
      r←(max⌊≢r)↑r
    ∇

    ∇ Ticker interval;conxs;data
    ⍝ every interval seconds, send a "tick" event (with an id) to every client of /clock
      :While ~Stopping
          {}⎕DL interval
          TickId+←1
          :If ~0∊⍴conxs←Server.SSEConnections'clock'
              (data←⎕NS'').(time clients)←(fmtTime ⎕TS)(≢conxs)
              {}conxs Server.SendSSE('tick'TickId)Server.FormatSSE data
          :EndIf
      :EndWhile
    ∇

:EndNamespace
